  "title": "Acceptance vs delinquency (production BNPL first)",
  "caption": "Top: production comparison on last-3-month BNPL traffic (95% CI ±2% sample). Blue = stored autogluon_v25; rust = locally scored union AF package 1 MSE on the same users; charcoal = selected challenger. Bottom: union Almost Full holdout (BNPL leftover + cards), delinquency = 1 − pngi_rate. Hover a Plotly chart for cutoff and rates. The original Fritz dashboard is unchanged.",
  "note_html": "\n<p><strong>Top row (production, BNPL only):</strong> stored <code>autogluon_v25</code> from\n<code>pre_scored_users</code>, the locally scored union Almost Full package 1 MSE on the same users\n(these two can differ), and the selected challenger. Sample is last-3-month BNPL\n<code>bnpl.api_requests</code> ∩ stored v25, sized for 95% confidence and ±2% error\n(Wald, p=0.5, finite-population correction). Delinquency = independent last-90-day matured BNPL CaaS draw.</p>\n<p><strong>Bottom row (holdout):</strong> gated yes-share of union <code>test_v25.csv</code>\n(BNPL leftover + cards, same 80/20 split as prior v25). Delinquency = labeled unpaid share\n<code>1 − pngi_rate</code> in the score tail — not Fritz CaaS pesos.\nThe original Fritz Pages copy is unchanged.</p>\n",
